{
  // part-tester: (top-level-login part-tester) runtime-constructs three
  // types via (new 'type ...) (test-process, part-tester, save-memcard),
  // each fed its own type-flag doubleword (size + method-count-derived flag
  // bits) the same lui/ori/addu far-label way as the scert family below.
  // L166 (0x100094/0x13) was the first "Failed to guess label use" hit; L164
  // (0x10009c/0xf) and L165 (0x800110/0x3b) are the other two, same shape.
  // L157 is an rgba static (0x80ffffff, white at half alpha) passed as the
  // color arg to add-debug-x, loaded whole via a 64-bit ld the same far-label
  // way as the type-flag doublewords above ("Failed to guess label use").
  "part-tester": [["L157", "rgba", true], ["L164", "uint64", true], ["L165", "uint64", true], ["L166", "uint64", true]],
  // scert-5-h/6-h/7-h/8-h/10-h: far-label uint64 flag doublewords reached via
  // lui/ori/addu; single-lane decomp-config, one marker each before this fix.
  // The decompiler only reports the first label-use failure per function, so
  // these are landed as full blocks rather than one entry at a time.
  //
  // Scoped decode confirms all five reach zero ERROR markers with this fix.
  // goal_src landing is deferred for all five: each references a medius-lobby
  // message-struct type not yet defined at its own game.gd compile position.
  // scert-5-h/7-h/8-h/10-h need net-address/net-address-list/net-connection-
  // info/rsa-key, which now live in net-mgr-h.gc (slot 131), but those four
  // scert files sit at slots 118-129, earlier in game.gd, so the types are
  // not visible yet (goalc-test's build-first variant fails even though
  // offline-test alone passes, since offline-test preloads all-types.gc
  // instead of replaying goal_src order). scert-6-h has no dependency on the
  // net-mgr-h family but hits a separate unlanded type, medius-player-
  // online-state (all-types.gc:24616), used inline by many medius message
  // structs. Resolving either chain is a type-dependency campaign, not a
  // one-fix landing; tracked as follow-up, not attempted this rung.
